The one patch Kickoff carries on iroh 1.3.0 (design §3.4, R2-10).

The IP transport's send path asks Kickoff's send guard before every packet,
so destinations iroh picks itself (NAT-traversal probes to candidates the
remote announces, path migration, QAD) pass the same policy as dials. The
guard lives in crates/send-guard, a dependency-free registry, because iroh
cannot depend on kickoff-net.

scripts/check-vendor.sh rebuilds vendor/iroh-1.3.0 from the crates.io archive
(pinned SHA-256) plus this file (pinned SHA-256) and fails on any other
difference. Changing this patch means changing both pins in that script.

--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -274,6 +274,9 @@
 version = "1.3.0"
 default-features = false
 
+[dependencies.kickoff-send-guard]
+path = "../../crates/send-guard"
+
 [dependencies.n0-error]
 version = "1.0.0"
 
--- a/src/socket/transports/ip.rs
+++ b/src/socket/transports/ip.rs
@@ -324,6 +324,12 @@
